Vercel Web Analytics Implementation
=====================================

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the polydebate project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

Changes Made:
-------------

1. **Package Installation:**
   - Installed @vercel/analytics@^2.0.1 using npm
   - Updated package.json to include the new dependency
   - Updated package-lock.json with resolved dependencies

2. **Analytics Integration:**
   - Modified: frontend/src/app/layout.tsx
   - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
   - Placed <Analytics /> component at the end of the <body> tag
   - This follows Next.js App Router best practices

Implementation Details:
-----------------------

The Analytics component was added to the root layout (src/app/layout.tsx) following the Next.js App Router pattern. The component is placed inside the <body> tag after all other content, which ensures:

- Analytics tracking is available across all pages automatically
- The component loads without blocking page rendering
- Proper integration with Next.js routing system
- Minimal impact on application performance

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router projects, ensuring compatibility with the project's framework (Next.js 16.0.10).

Testing & Verification:
------------------------

✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✅ No new linting errors introduced in modified files
✅ TypeScript compilation successful
✅ All 30 static routes generated without errors

Next Steps:
-----------

To activate Web Analytics:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics)
3. After deployment, verify tracking by checking the Network tab for analytics requests

The analytics will automatically track page views and user interactions once deployed to Vercel with the feature enabled in the dashboard.
